Srinivasan, 2000]. Keeping multiple product concept options open and freezing
the concept late in the development process affords the flexibility to respond to
market and technology shifts. It is possible to create static and dynamic virtual
prototypes that are displayed at a website for review and testing by suppliers,
customers, and designers. Virtual prototypes cost considerably less to build and
